cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: >-
  If you use this code or the recorded experiments, please cite the paper below.
title: >-
  LLM Agent-Based Design of RISC-V CPUs with FPGA-in-the-Loop Evaluation
authors:
  - family-names: Itoh
    given-names: Leo
    affiliation: The University of Tokyo
  - family-names: Kadomoto
    given-names: Junichiro
    affiliation: The University of Tokyo
abstract: >-
  A development environment in which LLM agents implement CPU candidates on an
  FPGA and use on-board performance measurements to guide design decisions,
  applied to the human-supervised development of a single-cycle RV32I core into
  a three-wide out-of-order RV32IM core. The final design reaches 5.61
  CoreMark/MHz at 130 MHz on an Artix-7 FPGA, and FPGA evaluation was 9.6x
  faster than single-threaded RTL simulation over 8,000 CoreMark iterations.
  Submitted to IEEE ISCAS 2027.
keywords:
  - RISC-V
  - FPGA
  - LLM agent
  - CPU design
  - out-of-order execution
  - electronic design automation
date-released: 2026-10-29
repository-code: https://github.com/kadomoto-lab/llm-cpu-fpga-loop
url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.39570
doi: 10.48550/arXiv.2610.39570
